# One host per line. Copy to deploy/hosts and edit.
#
# Each entry is an INDEPENDENT router with its own channel state. There is no
# shared bus, so do not put several of these behind one hostname: clients
# landing on different hosts would never hear each other. Give each its own
# name and let clients pick one.
#
# Anything ssh accepts works: a hostname, an alias from ~/.ssh/config, or
# user@host. deploy.sh connects as root.

router1.example.com
router2.example.com

# An ssh alias is often easier, so the key and port live in ~/.ssh/config:
# my-router-fra
